{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If set above "},{"code":"0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (exclusive), blends between the fog’s color and the color of the background "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Sky","isActive":true},{"text":", as read from the radiance cubemap. This has a small performance cost when set above ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0"},{"text":". Must have ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment\/backgroundMode","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" set to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment\/BGMode\/sky","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Environment\/fogAerialPerspective"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fogAerialPerspective","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful to simulate "},{"text":"aerial perspective","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" in large scenes with low density fog. However, it is not very useful for high-density fog, as the sky will shine through. When set to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0"},{"text":", the fog color comes completely from the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Sky","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". If set to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0"},{"type":"text","text":", aerial perspective is disabled."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Notice that this does not sample the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Sky"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, but rather the radiance cubemap. The cubemap is sampled at a mipmap level depending on the depth of the rendered pixel; the farther away, the higher the resolution of the sampled mipmap. This results in the actual color being a blurred version of the sky, with more blur closer to the camera. The highest mipmap resolution is used at a depth of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Camera3D\/far","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/environment\/fogaerialperspective"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fogAerialPerspective"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot11EnvironmentC20fogAerialPerspectiveSdvp","title":"fogAerialPerspective"},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Camera3D/far":{"kind":"symbol","title":"far","abstract":[{"text":"The distance to the far culling boundary for this camera relative to its local Z axis. Higher values allow the camera to see further away, while decreasing ","type"